course: dictionary
lesson: 15472
title: Stowaways: hidden travellers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stowaway is a person who hides on a ship, plane, train or lorry so they can travel without paying or without being allowed. The clues are in the sentence: «The stowaway hid in a lifeboat before the ship set sail.» They hid, and they were not allowed on board, so a stowaway is a hidden traveller.
explain: Stow away is a verb made of two words. It means to hide on a vehicle to travel secretly. «Tom stowed away in a lorry full of apples.» He hid, and nobody knew he was there. Stows away, stowed away and stowing away are the other forms, and a stowaway is the person who does it.
explain: Stowaway can also be playful. It can mean an animal or thing that travelled by accident. «A tiny frog was a stowaway in the box of bananas.» The frog did not plan a trip, and it arrived in the shop without anyone knowing. Ask yourself: did someone hide on purpose, or did something just travel by accident?
fact: A stowaway is someone who hides on a ship, plane, train or lorry to travel without permission.
fact: Stow away (verb) means to hide on a vehicle to travel secretly. The plural noun is stowaways.
fact: «The stowaway hid behind the crates.» Here the clues are hid and behind the crates.
fact: Stowing away is very dangerous and against the law.
fact: Playful meaning: a stowaway can be an animal or thing that travelled by accident, like a spider in a box of bananas.
exercise: «The stowaway hid behind the crates until the ship had left the harbour.» What is a stowaway? | A ship's captain | A sailor who is paid to load the crates | *A person who hides on a vehicle to travel without permission | A type of crate
exercise: «Last night, two boys stowed away on a lorry.» What does stowed away mean? | To drive the lorry very fast | To unload the lorry at the shop | *To hide on a vehicle to travel secretly | To wash the lorry
exercise: «A tiny spider was a stowaway in the box of bananas.» What does stowaway mean here? | *A spider that travelled by accident | A spider that lived in the shop for years | A spider that was sold to a customer | A spider that was painted
test: «The cat was a stowaway on the train, hidden under a seat until the end of the journey.» What is the cat? | A guard who checked the tickets | *Someone or something that hid on the train to travel without being allowed | A pet that was given a ticket | A lost animal that was sitting on the platform
test: «Stowing away on a plane is dangerous and against the law.» What does this sentence tell you? | Planes are always safe for hidden passengers | *Hiding on a plane to travel is risky and not allowed | Planes never carry any luggage | Stowing away is a fun game for children
exam: Ben reads, «The stowaway was found in the lifeboat after the ship had sailed.» What does the word tell you about the person? | They were the ship's captain | They were a lifeboat rescuer | They were paying for a ticket | *They hid on the ship without permission
